* Filamentary ReRAM driven by a +-1.6 V, 5meg Hz sinusoid for two periods: one point of the
* frequency fingerprint (decks reram_freq_5k, _500k, _5meg; numbers in
* docs/multiphysics.md and docs/examples/multiphysics/reram_loops.py, which draws the loops).
* A memristor's pinched loop shrinks as the drive outruns its state: the gap is moved by
* thermally activated ion drift, which completes within a half period at 5 kHz, only partly at
* 500 kHz, and hardly at all at 5 MHz.
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/reram_freq_5meg.net --model models/multiphysics/reram --tran --report in,te,X1.g
V1 in gnd SIN(0 1.6 5meg)
R1 in te 2k
X1 te gnd reram
.tran 10p 0.4u
.end
